; @ARCHIVE@ uninstall: removes what its Install put in. The base's Uninstall
; runs the copy of this script in @RECORD@ before it removes the base.
; Run from anywhere:  Execute Uninstall
FailAt 21
; @include dist/addons/@ID@/uninstall-body.dos
; @include dist/common/@ADDONVAR@
; the record: its copy of this script is the one a base Uninstall is running, which
; AmigaDOS cannot delete while it is read (the base removes it with its own drawer)
Delete >NIL: "@RECORD@" ALL QUIET
Echo "@ARCHIVE@ removed."
